# News refresh workflow

When the user asks to complete/update **news** articles (e.g. "nuevas noticias", "completar artículos"):

## Research

1. Search the web for **recent** news per **active** game hub (`neverness-to-everness`, `animal-crossing-new-horizons`, `stardew-valley`).
2. Prefer: version updates, new characters, events, official patch notes, credible gaming press.
3. Skip duplicates — read existing `src/content/articles/*.md` for that `gameSlug` first.

## Add content

- Add **1–2 new** `category: news` articles per game (or as many as the user specifies).
- Lists use **`publishedAt` newest first** (`getNewsByGame` / `getGuidesByGame` sort desc).
- File: `src/content/articles/{slug}.md` — cozy magazine tone per `docs/EDITORIAL.md`, not tier-list speak.
- Frontmatter: `title`, `excerpt`, `gameSlug`, `publishedAt` (YYYY-MM-DD), `readTime`, `seo.title`, `seo.description`.
- Optional: `featured`, `trending`, `coverImage`, `coverCaption`.

## Images

- Put assets under `public/images/games/{game-slug}/` (often `news/` or `inspiration/`).
- **Every news article needs a unique `coverImage`** within its `gameSlug` — never reuse `cover.jpg` / `header.jpg` across multiple cards (they are often the same asset).
- Inline body images must differ from the hero `coverImage`.
- Add `<figure class="article-inline-figure">` when useful; note source in caption or footer when not original.

## Verify

- Run `npm run content:lint` — duplicate or hero=inline covers **fail** the lint.
- Do not commit unless the user asks.
